.SH NAME
niac-list-walks - List SNMP walk files


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac list walks [vendor-or-prefix] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List SNMP walk files from the content library. If a prefix is
provided, only matching walk paths are shown. This mirrors the Java demo
wrapper's vendor browsing flow while preserving Go's library layout.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for walks


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--root\fP=""
	Library root (default: NIAC_LIBRARY_ROOT or ~/.niac/library)

.PP
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # List all SNMP walks
  niac list walks

  # List Cisco walks
  niac list walks cisco
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-list(1)\fP


